# Cursor AI Agent Guidelines

This repository enforces an **AI-Native Orchestrator-Subagent Framework**. The Single Source of Truth (SSOT) is located in the `.ai/` directory.

## Core Directives
1. **SSOT Master Router**: Read and follow [.ai/README.md](../../.ai/README.md) for complete architecture, roles, and guidelines.
2. **Orchestrator Protocol**: Multi-file or complex changes must follow the Orchestrator loop defined in [.ai/agents/orchestrator.md](../../.ai/agents/orchestrator.md) and [.ai/rules/orchestration-protocol.md](../../.ai/rules/orchestration-protocol.md).
3. **TypeScript Standards**:
   - Strict ESM: all relative imports must include `.js` extension.
   - Always use `Number.parseInt(str, 10)` and `Number.parseFloat(str)`.
   - No `any` types; use Zod `safeParse`.
   - See [.ai/rules/typescript-standards.md](../../.ai/rules/typescript-standards.md).
4. **Security & Workflows**:
   - Zero high/critical CVEs (`npm audit`).
   - Pin third-party GitHub Actions to 40-character commit SHAs.
   - See [.ai/rules/security-policies.md](../../.ai/rules/security-policies.md) and [.ai/rules/action-workflow-rules.md](../../.ai/rules/action-workflow-rules.md).
5. **Verification**:
   - Always run verification playbook [.ai/skills/build-and-verify/SKILL.md](../../.ai/skills/build-and-verify/SKILL.md):
     `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run test:coverage`
